'''Coruxón Station''' is a major railway station in the [[Coruxón]] [[Cantons of Balisca|borough]] in [[Castejón]], [[Balisca]]. Serving as the main connecting hub for rail traffic between Castejón's and the rest of the [[Concordia|Concordia megalopolis]] on the {{W|inter-city rail}}, {{W|commuter rail}}, and {{W|rapid transit|subway}} lines. The station was used by an average of 2.5 million people per day in 2022, making it, by far, Balisca's busiest station. 

Outside of its role as a transit hub, Coruxón Station is often used as a meeting place, and is especially featured in films and television. It contains a variety of amenities and services such as {{W|capsule hotels}} and {{W|sleep pods}}, {{W|cannabis store|cannabis cooperatives}}, coffee shops and other food vendors, including upscale restaurants and bars, a food hall, and a grocery marketplace. 

